
	
	docker compose up -d (up: Tells docker to read the YAML file and start everything inside, -d: Runs it in the background)
	
	docker compose down (Stops everything, frees up the RAM instantly).
	
	docker compose down --rmi all (removes the images too if you're low disk space).
	
	docker compose stop (Pause everything, saves CPU but keeps the containers).

	docker compose ps (See exactly what's running and which ports they use).

	docker compose logs -f (See the live "heartbeat"(logs) of your servers).

